        "identifier": "https://github.com/google-deepmind/formal-conjectures/blob/b6939a3a0d89e5f999fa8c6483a6ef646c1e2923/FormalConjectures/OpenQuantumProblems/35.lean",
        "note": "Supplies the statement `ame_12_5_open` and every definition it uses. Challenge.lean copies the definitions the statement uses, and the statement, verbatim, with Formal Conjectures' names; AME125/Defs.lean copies the file up to its benchmark statements, with the `category` and `AMS` attributes removed and Mathlib imported in place of Formal Conjectures' own library. In both, one proof step inside combineFirst is `exact Nat.sub_lt_sub_right him i.2` instead of Formal Conjectures' `omega` (see fidelity); audit/Audit.lean keeps Formal Conjectures' original under another name and checks by rfl that the two are equal. scripts/check-fc-match.py checks all of this against Formal Conjectures at that commit. An earlier version of this proof depended on Formal Conjectures directly (commit 9833012f) and was linked from Formal Conjectures PR #7539.",
